nt path you see  most people on LinkedIn generally want  to get paid for their work with money  but Marcus didn't have any money left he  was completely broke so instead Marcus  did what all great entrepreneurs do he  posted the software engineering job ad  on an obscure PHP software developer  upper Forum he got just one response  from an engineer named Oliver was  literally two sentences looking for a  developer a contact email that was it  now Oliver's resume might not look all  that impressive he doesn't have many  LinkedIn connections and instead of  experience at a fancy tech company  Oliver had only worked for a small local  software development agency he designed  an online music store a News website for  a city in Spain as well as a website  that offered to help you increase the  odds of picking winning lottery numbers  now none of these projects are visually  stunning they all scream late 2000's web  design but you should never judge an  introverted software engineer by their  LinkedIn profile as Marcus got to know  Oliver he realized that he was talking  to one of the best developers in Estonia  and made him a co-founder it was the  opportunity of a lifetime and one that  Oliver had been preparing for since he  started coding at the age of eight in a  matter of weeks Oliver built a working  version of the app which put the  company's expansion plans on more solid  ground sound and I got hooked on the  technical aspect of it also it was so  interesting thing to boil because  there's so many different aspects of  building you know this real-time  application none of the founders took a  salary for the first six months and even  later on they continued to operate on a  shoestring budget but their sacrifice  was worth it just eight months in Bolt  had become the local market leader doing  50 000 rides per month and generating 7  000 Euros per month in revenue from taxi  companies but most of the challenges  that both had to overcome still lay  ahead when Marc